@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@ It is a rulebook, not a changelog.
 - Every table has an `id` column, except join tables with a composite key. Its value is
   `newEntityId("<ENTITY>")` from `@lib/db-models`; a new table adds its uppercase prefix to
   `ENTITY_PREFIXES` there first.
+- **Analytics has one emitter per fact** ([docs/analytics.md](docs/analytics.md)): the
+  Worker reports state changes with `analytics` from `@lib/analytics-server`, where the
+  change is made; the browser reports only intent. Never track from a frontend mutation
+  hook, and never put an email, id or token in an event property.
 - Server code logs a **constant message** with everything variable as a property
   (`log.info("user created", { userId })`); never put emails, passwords or tokens in a
   property.
